  "review_notes": [
    "Egyptian brand names سيتال (Cetal, paracetamol) and اسبوسيد (Aspocid, aspirin) are from memory; please verify.",
    "'pain' is generic and its match patterns overlap with every specific pain; the checker treats it as weak evidence only.",
    "German 'verstopft' is deliberately NOT a match pattern, because 'die Nase ist verstopft' is a stuffy nose, not constipation.",
    "German 'schlecht' alone is NOT a nausea pattern, because of 'ich krieg schlecht Luft'.",
    "Egyptian 'نفسي' alone is NOT a pattern: it appears in nausea (غمم نفس), appetite (نفسي مسدودة) and breath (آخد نفسي).",
    "Egyptian 'دايخ/دايخة' is mapped to dizziness only (literal meaning). Colloquially it may also describe nausea; this ambiguity is a known limitation.",
    "'نهجان' was removed from ar_eg after native-speaker review (not used in Egyptian Arabic)."
  ]
}